# `text.charAt(i) === ","` makes no text of one character: the byte is compared with 44. The loop for 8-bit characters is written out eight times.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 8
# REPEAT: turn = 1..8
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[unit%(turn)]] = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:characters8,
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isComma%(turn)]] = Equal(b@[[unit%(turn)]], $44(
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isComma%(turn)]], Terminal,
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:Unlikely:#
# END REPEAT
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop

# No range check, no test of the width or for a rope, no poll, no load out of the table of one-character texts, no comparison of texts.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 8
# HOT-NOT: isLoopPoll
# HOT-NOT: Reads:StringImpl
# HOT-NOT: Reads:JSRopeString
# HOT-NOT: Reads:singleCharacterStrings
# HOT-NOT: Reads:{
# HOT-NOT: ExitsSideways
# HOT-NOT: Below(
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop

# x86-64 compares the byte in memory. ARM64 loads it first.
# X64: instructions: 3, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
# X64: instructions: 10, patchpoints: 8, {{*}} steps by 8
# ARM64: instructions: 4, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
# ARM64: instructions: 19, patchpoints: 8, {{*}} steps by 8
